ial on the deformation path. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.AWDeformationPath.free_qHermite_bottom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.AWDeformationPath.free_qHermite_bottom","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/AWDeformationPath.lean#L42-L42","doc":"the free endpoint is the q-Hermite bottom of the scheme:\nthe diagonal term vanishes at `t = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.AWDeformationPath.c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.AWDeformationPath.c","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/AWDeformationPath.lean#L39-L39","doc":"deformation family: sub-diagonal at parameter `t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.AWDeformationPath.b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.AWDeformationPath.b","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/AWDeformationPath.lean#L37-L37","doc":"deformation family: diagonal at parameter `t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.AWDeformationPath.a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.AWDeformationPath.a","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/AWDeformationPath.lean#L35-L35","doc":"deformation family: super-diagonal at parameter `t` (units, matching\n`overlapColumn`/`IsEigencolumn`, so each `t`-slice plugs into the\noverlap machinery without extra plumbing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.AWDeformationPath.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.AWDeformationPath.mk","kind":"ctor","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/AWDeformationPath.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.AWDeformationPath","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.AWDeformationPath","kind":"class","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/AWDeformationPath.lean#L23-L60","doc":"**AW deformation-path conjecture (§3b class; conjecture — no instance\nis provided).**  One AW tridiagonal family `(a t, b t, c t)` joins the\nfree endpoint (`t = 0`, q-Hermite bottom: diagonal off) to the bound\nendpoint (`t = 1`); a potential `Φ` on the path has the complex-volume\ndefect `𝔙` as its endpoint difference (the categorical Neumann–Zagier\npath integral); and the `𝔙`-ladder satisfies ONE three-term recurrence\nwhose multiplier is **bar-even**.  All fields are inputs; the\ntwo-channel (binding + `𝔔_β`) descent is derived below. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:complex-volume-character-variety-path","label":"rem:complex-volume-character-variety-path","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/complex-volume-character-variety-path.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}